# caravan_meet_witness.rish -- Caravan meet witness.
#
# `owe.rye` opened the last door: a concession the plan made is written down as a
# debt that outlives the run that made it, addressed forward to a run that has
# not started. So the admission finally costs the plan something past the breath
# that spoke it -- and then the run after it opens, reads nothing, and settles
# whole.
#
#   THE RUN THAT INHERITS A DEBT IS MADE TO MEET IT.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, MEASURED:
#
#   * THE NUMBER THE TWO PLANS DISAGREE ON IS DEBTS A PLAN INHERITED THAT THE RUN
#     NEVER MET. Both runs open holding the same debt an earlier run booked, both
#     carry the same case to the same desk, both read the same hand's answer,
#     both publish the same finding, and both take that finding on the record in
#     the same words. What parts them is whether the admission they opened
#     holding is ever met. It falls from 1 to 0.
#   * MEETING COMES BEFORE BOOKING, AND THE ORDERING IS THE RUNG. The debt on the
#     wire is the debt this run inherited right up until the moment this run
#     writes its own, so a run that booked first would meet today's concession
#     and call yesterday's answered. This is the first rung of the arc whose
#     place in the order is a safety property rather than a courtesy.
#   * A RUN MEETS THE DEBT THAT ACTUALLY STOOD. The debt this lap seats is
#     deliberately unlike anything either measured run would book of its own --
#     taken over a finding that went FOR the plan, under an outcome already
#     reporting itself short -- so a receipt naming those two bytes can only be a
#     receipt for the inherited debt. `MeetMismatched` is the rung itself,
#     refused by name on metal.
#   * MEETING IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE WORK THIS RUN DID. A run that has published no
#     outcome of its own has met nothing, however willing it was, and
#     `MeetUnsettled` refuses by name. `MeetUnowed` refuses where no debt stood
#     at all, since a run cannot answer an admission nobody made.
#   * A RECEIPT CARRIES TWO BYTES -- the debt met, echoed back exactly as it
#     stood, so a later reader can lay the two beside each other and see that the
#     admission answered is the admission that stood.
#   * THE TAKING DOWN IS THE ACT; THE RECEIPT IS ITS RemainingRECEIPT. A meeting written
#     beside a debt still standing would have every run after this one inherit an
#     admission already answered, and answer it again.
#   * A RECEIPT SURVIVES A PROVISIONING, AND THE DEBT IT ANSWERS STAYS DOWN --
#     proven as its own fold, since a receipt swept every morning would have the
#     same admission met forever, and a debt that came back with the morning
#     would make the meeting a courtesy rather than a close.
#   * A PLAN INHERITING NOTHING MEETS NOTHING, proven on the wire as its own run.
#     Only a standing admission can be answered.
#   * MEETING IS NOT REPAIRING, AND IT IS NOT CONCEDING TWICE. The receipt says
#     the inherited admission was finally looked at; it never decides what the
#     look found. Both runs settle `carried out whole`, both leave the quarrel
#     standing where its holder left it, both leave the age at 4 and the standing
#     loud, both leave the same case on the same desk, both publish the same
#     finding, both take that finding on the record, and both leave today's own
#     concession owing nothing.
#   * FIVE REFUSALS THIS RUNG EARNS, matching the five below it. `MeetUnowed` is
#     the moment a debt is met at all. `MeetUnsettled` is whether this run has
#     earned a word about it. `MeetMismatched` is the whole point.
#     `MeetMiscounted` is the honesty of the count: every debt inherited is met
#     or left deferred, never both and never neither. `MeetMisrecorded` is the
#     record, read back both ways -- the receipt written where a later run finds
#     it, and the debt itself finally down.
#   * A PLAN KEEPING ITS OWN WORD OWES NOTHING, a plan that says nothing concedes
#     nothing, a run owed no word from anybody answers none, a plan nobody ever
#     pressed a quarrel against is answered by nobody, and a desk that has said
#     nothing yet leaves the case honestly waiting -- each carried whole from the
#     rungs below. A plan that loses nothing still reads as the line handed, all
#     16 pairs, this arc's standing generalization test one tier further out.
#
# Six RED paths were proven on metal before this witness claimed GREEN. Skip the
# write and keep the read-back armed and the run refuses `MeetMisrecorded`. Write
# the receipt and leave the debt standing and it refuses `MeetMisrecorded` again,
# from the second read-back. Read the wire as holding nothing and it refuses
# `MeetUnowed`. Read the settlement as unpublished and it refuses
# `MeetUnsettled`. File the receipt against some other admission and it refuses
# `MeetMismatched` -- the rung itself. Count one debt as both met and deferred
# and it refuses `MeetMiscounted`. Disarm every guard at once -- the write
# skipped, the taking down skipped, both read-backs dropped, and the harness's
# own two reads removed -- and the selftest calls itself GREEN while
# `caravan/.meets/plan.met` does not exist at all and the inherited debt is still
# standing, so an operator would believe an admission had been answered that
# nobody ever looked at. Seeing that is what makes the reading back a check
# rather than decoration.
#
# Checks read the selftest output natively (`contains`), never a shell grep over
# interpolated output -- REDS %76 / %85, the apostrophe loom.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ca/caravan_meet_witness.rish

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "caravan/bin/meet"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p caravan/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/meet.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]

assert build.ok else "caravan meet build failed -- ${build.err}"

# The reader this witness runs is built here rather than borrowed (REDS %92).
let read_bin_build = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/read.rye -femit-bin=caravan/bin/meet_read"]
assert read_bin_build.ok else "caravan read build failed -- ${read_bin_build.err}"

# The board declaration the rungs below opened, unchanged.
let published = run ["sh" "-c" "caravan/bin/meet_read caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron 2>&1"]
assert published.ok else "the board declaration could not be read"
assert published.out contains "domains 4 -- channels 3 -- regions 11 -- grants 22" else "the board declaration changed shape"
assert published.out contains "verdict: whole" else "the board declaration did not read whole"

# A fresh start for the stores, the doorbells, this plan's notes, and the boxes
# outside it. Every quarrel, every finding, and every debt this witness reads was
# seated by the lap itself, standing in for the runs that met this argument
# before today.
let clean = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf caravan/.regions caravan/.channels caravan/.meets caravan/.readers"]
assert clean.ok else "the region stores, doorbells, notes, and outside boxes could not be cleared"

let test = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert test.ok else "caravan meet selftest exited non-zero"
assert test.out contains "GREEN" else "caravan meet selftest not GREEN"
assert test.out contains "the run that inherits a debt is made to meet it" else "the meet finding did not close"

# The meeting and its five refusals, read straight, before any dependent runs.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unowed, unsettled, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five meet refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "the plan opens holding a debt, and closes still holding it" else "a bare plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the plan meets the debt it inherited, and takes it down" else "a meeting plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a receipt carries two bytes: the debt met, echoed back exactly as it stood" else "a receipt did not name what it carries"

# The property that makes a receipt worth writing, proven as its own fold: it
# outlives the run that made it, and the debt it answers does not come back.
assert test.out contains "a receipt survives a provisioning, and the debt it answers stays down" else "a receipt was never proven past a provisioning"

# The ending this rung reaches by writing nothing at all, on the wire.
assert test.out contains "a plan inheriting nothing meets nothing, and writes no receipt" else "a plan holding no debt was credited with meeting one"

# The owing below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unsaid, unconceded, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five owe refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "the plan concedes, and owes nothing when the run is over" else "the owing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a debt carries two bytes: the finding conceded, and the outcome conceded under" else "a debt did not name what it carries"
assert test.out contains "a debt survives a provisioning, and falls with the concession it carries" else "a debt was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "a plan keeping its own word owes the work nothing, and books nothing" else "a dissenting plan was made to owe the work a look"
assert test.out contains "a plan that says nothing concedes nothing, and books nothing" else "a silent plan left a debt standing anyway"

# The avowing below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unheard, unfound, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five avow refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "an avowal carries two bytes: the finding it answers, and the plan's word on it" else "an avowal did not name what it carries"
assert test.out contains "the plan takes the finding, and says the work is owed another look" else "a plan conceding did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a word survives a provisioning, and falls with the finding it answers" else "a word was never proven past a provisioning"

# The three endings the rungs below reach by publishing nothing, each on the wire.
assert test.out contains "a run owed no word from anybody publishes none" else "a plan that carried no case out answered a finding"
assert test.out contains "a plan nobody ever pressed a quarrel against is answered by nobody" else "a plan nobody pressed was answered all the same"
assert test.out contains "a desk that has said nothing yet leaves the case honestly waiting" else "a silent desk did not leave the case waiting"

# The reading below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "the hand the case went to is read back, and its finding published" else "the reading below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a finding survives a provisioning, and belongs to the hand that wrote it" else "a finding was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unreferred, silent, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the deem refusals stopped standing"

# The referring below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "a long-standing quarrel is put before a hand that is neither party" else "the referring below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a case survives a provisioning, and outlives the quarrel it was built from" else "a case was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: early, unaddressed, party, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the refer refusals stopped standing"

# The swelling, the dwelling, and every rung beneath them, unchanged.
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a long-standing quarrel reads where the outcome is read" else "the swelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a standing survives a provisioning, and falls with the quarrel it speaks for" else "a standing was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "an age climbs by the run just stood and never shortens" else "the dwelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "an age survives a provisioning, and falls with the quarrel it counts" else "an age was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "a quarrel comes down on its holder's word and on nobody else's" else "the relenting below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads under the quarrel it inherited" else "the heeding below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a pressed quarrel outlives the run that heard it" else "the endurance below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads what its reader says back" else "the appeal below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it writes back to the reader who objected" else "the tidings below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its marks carry the standing of their objection" else "the standing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes how long the objection beside its word may stand" else "the term below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its word is read beside the reading against it" else "the escort below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its record may hold a disagreement" else "the record below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it hears what its reader answers" else "the hearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections travel" else "the delivery below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections are addressed" else "the amendment below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own judgments answer to a later run" else "the recantation below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan names what it expects of a phase, and what it would accept of a loss" else "the bearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a repair still refuses by name: unread, whole, overreaching" else "the mend below stopped being weighed"

# The generalization test the whole arc keeps.
assert test.out contains "a plan that loses nothing reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs" else "an unlost plan did not read as the line handed"

# The meeting lap: one plan run twice over a debt an earlier run booked and left
# standing in its own notes. Every number stands still -- the work, the
# dependents, the correction, the journey, the record, the escort, the asking,
# the mark, the telling, the position carried forward, the word standing under
# it, the age, the standing, the case, the finding, the plan's own answer, the
# concession it left owing nothing, the settlement -- and only the meeting moves.
assert test.out contains "phases: 6 deferred, 6 met" else "the two plans ran different records"
assert test.out contains "dependents: 6 deferred, 6 met" else "meeting a debt cost work it should not have"
assert test.out contains "phases absorbed into a standing dependent: 3 deferred, 3 met" else "the two plans absorbed different phases"
assert test.out contains "abandoned reach, conferred and never served: 3 deferred, 3 met" else "the two plans lost different work"
assert test.out contains "phases re-seated to carry what was lost: 3 deferred, 3 met" else "the two plans repaired different work"
assert test.out contains "standing judgments taken back on this run's own evidence: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the recanting rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readings corrected where they were read: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the amending rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "corrections carried to the place their reader was reached: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the couriering rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "disagreements written into the record: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the disputing rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published words standing beside the reading against them: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the abiding rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing objections put back to the reader who raised them: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the lapsing rung stopped asking under both plans"
assert test.out contains "marks carrying the standing of the objection they quote: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the standing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "raisers told how their own quarrel came out: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the tidings below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readers whose reply to the answer was read back: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the appeal below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "positions carried past the run that heard them: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "a run whose reader still presses dropped their position"
assert test.out contains "inherited positions weighed into the run's own word: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the regard stopped standing under a live quarrel"
assert test.out contains "standing positions left exactly where they were found: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the relenting below stopped leaving the position standing"
assert test.out contains "standing positions this run said the age of: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the dwelling below stopped dating under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing quarrels published where the outcome is read: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the swelling below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels carried to a hand that is neither party: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the referring below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "carried cases whose answer was read and published: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the reading below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published findings the plan answered on the record: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "the avowing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "findings a plan published and never said one word about: 0 against 0" else "a run left a finding it published unanswered"
assert test.out contains "concessions left owing nothing to any run after: 1 deferred, 1 met" else "meeting an old debt changed what today's word owed"
assert test.out contains "concessions a plan made that reach no run after them: 1 against 1" else "the two plans differed on today's own concession"
assert test.out contains "inherited debts this run met and took down: 0 deferred, 1 met" else "the meeting did not part the two plans"
assert test.out contains "inherited debts left standing for the run after: 1 deferred, 0 met" else "the other half of the count did not close"
assert test.out contains "debts a plan inherited that the run never met: 1 against 0" else "the two plans left the same admission unmet"
assert test.out contains "work still standing when the supervisor exits: 0 deferred, 0 met" else "the two plans left different work standing"
assert test.out contains "the plan, as an operator finally reads it: carried out whole deferred, carried out whole met" else "meeting a debt decided what the work came to"
assert test.out contains "breaks a named turn: 0 deferred, 0 met" else "the meeting run broke an order its author named"

# What an operator reads is what the wire carries. Every note is read here,
# outside the run that wrote it, exactly as each would be read by the person it
# was written for.
let settled = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.settled"]
assert settled.ok else "the plan published no settlement an operator could read"
assert settled.out contains "c" else "the wire did not carry the carried settlement the repair earned"

# The note this rung writes: the receipt for an admission finally looked at. Its
# two bytes are the inherited debt echoed back exactly -- a finding that went for
# the plan, under an outcome already reporting itself short -- which is nothing
# either measured run would ever have booked of its own.
let receipt = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.met"]
assert receipt.ok else "a meeting run left the inherited debt unanswered after all"
assert receipt.out contains "os" else "the receipt did not name the debt this run opened holding"

# And the act the receipt is only the record of: the debt is down, so no run
# after this one inherits an admission already answered.
let owed = run ["sh" "-c" "test -e caravan/.meets/plan.owe && echo standing || echo down"]
assert owed.ok else "the debt note could not be weighed"
assert owed.out contains "down" else "a meeting run wrote a receipt and left the debt standing"

# The word below it, untouched by the old debt met beside it.
let avowal = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.avow"]
assert avowal.ok else "the plan published no word of its own an operator could read"
assert avowal.out contains "ua" else "a meeting run rewrote the word it was only asked to leave alone"

# The finding below it, untouched.
let finding = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.deem"]
assert finding.ok else "the plan published no finding an operator could read"
assert finding.out contains "u" else "a meeting run rewrote the finding beneath it"

# The hand that wrote it still holds their own word, in their own box.
let answer = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.deem"]
assert answer.ok else "the hand outside the argument kept no answer of their own"
assert answer.out contains "cl" else "a meeting run reached onto a third hand's desk"

let case = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.case"]
assert case.ok else "no third hand was ever handed the case"
assert case.out contains "cl" else "a meeting run rewrote the case it had already carried out"

let forum = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.forum"]
assert forum.ok else "the plan named no hand outside the argument at all"
assert forum.out contains "bench" else "the wire did not name the third hand this lap seated"

# And the reader who raised the quarrel wrote no finding, which is the arc.
let unspoken = run ["sh" "-c" "test -e caravan/.readers/desk.deem && echo present || echo absent"]
assert unspoken.ok else "the reader box could not be weighed"
assert unspoken.out contains "absent" else "a party to the argument wrote the finding on it"

# The standing, the age, and the quarrel itself, each untouched.
let standing = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.swell"]
assert standing.ok else "the standing note could not be read at all"
assert standing.out contains "l" else "a quarrel four runs old did not read as long-standing"

let age = run ["sh" "-c" "od -An -tu1 caravan/.meets/plan.dwell | tr -d ' '"]
assert age.ok else "the age note could not be read at all"
assert age.out contains "4" else "a meeting run rewrote the age it was only asked to read"

let quarrel_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.standing"]
assert quarrel_note.ok else "a meeting run took down the position it never weighed"
assert quarrel_note.out contains "p" else "the position standing over the plan changed under a meeting run"

let regard = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.regard"]
assert regard.ok else "the regard note could not be read at all"
assert regard.out contains "u" else "an answered quarrel stopped standing over the plan's own word"

# The reader's own hand, in their own box, outside this plan's wire entirely --
# still pressing, which is exactly why their quarrel goes on standing.
let press = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.press"]
assert press.ok else "the reader replied nothing at all"
assert press.out contains "p" else "the holder of this lap's quarrel did not read as still pressing"

let plea = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.appeal"]
assert plea.ok else "the plan published no plea an operator could read"
assert plea.out contains "p" else "the record and the reader's own hand read differently"

let address = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.at"]
assert address.ok else "the plan kept no address for the reader who took its word"
assert address.out contains "desk" else "the wire did not name the place its reader was reached"

let beside = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.beside"]
assert beside.ok else "a run withdrew the mark its reader earned"
assert beside.out contains "s" else "the mark did not name the reading its reader holds"

let dispute = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.dispute"]
assert dispute.ok else "an open record kept no disagreement at all"
assert dispute.out contains "cs" else "the record did not name the plan's reading and its reader's"

let correction = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.amend"]
assert correction.ok else "the plan published no correction an operator could read"
assert correction.out contains "bc" else "the wire did not name the two readings the correction stands between"

let box = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.told"]
assert box.ok else "the reader's own box was never written to"
assert box.out contains "bc" else "the reader's box did not carry the correction in the words they read"

let outof = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.outof"]
assert outof.ok else "the raiser of the quarrel was never told how it came out"
assert outof.out contains "t" else "a word that never moved was reported to its raiser as one that did"

let recant_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.recant"]
assert recant_note.ok else "the plan published no recantation an operator could read"
assert recant_note.out contains ".r...." else "the wire did not name the one judgment this run took back"

let lost_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.meets/plan.lost"]
assert lost_note.ok else "the plan published no loss an operator could read"
assert lost_note.out contains ".x.x.x" else "the wire did not name the three phases the plan lost"

# The dependents measure the loss in their own hands, exactly as the rungs below
# left them, and the follower that once spoke for the judgment falls with it.
assert test.out contains "falls as its author declared, holding 1 conferred arcs it never served" else "a falling dependent did not fall holding its conferral"
assert test.out contains "client_b: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 1 conferred, 0 returned, 1 still reachable at home" else "the dependent a conferral was made to did not read it as its own"
assert test.out contains "client_c: bytes differed" else "the follower that once spoke for the judgment came home after all"

say "GREEN: Caravan meet witness passed."
